.TH MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-notify \- publish an event to the Mu2e DAQ notification server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-notify
[\fB\-\-server\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-fallback\-server\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-discover\fR]
.B send
[\fB\-\-severity\fR \fILEVEL\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-category\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-meta\fR \fIKEY\fB=\fIVALUE\fR]...
.I TITLE
.RI [ MESSAGE ]
.br
.B mu2edaq-notify
[\fB\-\-server\fR \fIURL\fR] [\fB\-\-fallback\-server\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-discover\fR]
.B ping
.SH DESCRIPTION
Command\-line publisher and health probe for
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1),
built on the
.BR mu2edaq_notify (3)
Python library.
.PP
.B send
publishes one event with
.BR "POST /api/events" .
.B ping
fetches
.B GET /api/health
and prints the JSON reply; it sends no token.
.PP
Two addresses are resolved, each in the order option > environment >
discovery: the primary
.RB ( \-\-server ,
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL ,
then the host/port/scheme of a mu2edaq\-discovery ANNOUNCE for
.BR app=notify )
and the fallback
.RB ( \-\-fallback\-server ,
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL ,
then that ANNOUNCE's
.BR meta.fallback_url ).
Discovery runs only when
.B mu2edaq_discovery
is importable and
.B \-\-no\-discover
is not given. The fallback is tried only when the primary cannot be reached
at the network level (DNS, connection, timeout, TLS); any HTTP reply,
including 4xx and 5xx, ends the attempt.
.PP
HTTPS certificates are verified (against the
.B certifi
bundle when installed, else the system store) and there is no option to
disable verification, so the URL must name a host the server certificate
covers: a server whose certificate is for its public name rejects
.BR https://localhost:8095 .
.PP
The bearer token is sent to whichever address is used, including an address
learned from discovery. Discovery replies are unauthenticated; pass
.B \-\-server
explicitly when the token matters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-server " URL"
Primary server base URL, e.g.
.BR https://mu2edaq-pager.fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-\-fallback\-server " URL"
Address to try when the primary is unreachable.
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Publisher API bearer token. Default
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN .
Without one no Authorization header is sent, which the server accepts only
when it has no tokens configured.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-discover
Do not query mu2edaq\-discovery.
.TP
.BI \-\-severity " LEVEL"
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.B warning
(default),
.BR error ,
or
.BR critical .
Any other value is a usage error.
.TP
.BI \-\-source " NAME"
Publishing application name (default
.BR cli ).
Filter rules match on it.
.TP
.BI \-\-category " NAME"
Subsystem tag, e.g. Trigger or Tracker. Default
.BR $MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY ,
else none. Freeform: the server's
.B GET /api/categories
lists the configured set, but any value is accepted.
.TP
.BI \-\-meta " KEY" = VALUE
Attach a metadata pair; repeatable. An argument without
.B =
becomes a key with an empty value.
.TP
.I TITLE
Short title, shown as the push banner (truncated to 200 characters).
.TP
.I MESSAGE
Detail body (truncated to 4000 characters). If
.I TITLE
and
.I MESSAGE
are both empty the command fails with a Python
.BR ValueError .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_URL
Primary server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_FALLBACK_URL
Fallback server URL.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN
Publisher bearer token.
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CATEGORY
Default category for
.BR send .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Event accepted (2xx), or health check answered.
.TP
.B 1
Event rejected or no server reachable; for
.BR ping ,
no configured or discovered server answered.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, or no subcommand given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish an error with an explicit server and token:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-notify \-\-server https://mu2edaq\-pager.fnal.gov \e
    \-\-token "$MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_TOKEN" send \-\-severity error \e
    \-\-source dtc\-monitor \-\-category Trigger \e
    \-\-meta run=107001 "DTC link down" "ROC link 3 lost lock"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Find the server by discovery and check it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-notify ping
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1),
.BR mu2edaq_notify (3),
.BR mu2edaq_notify_cpp (3)
.PP
.I docs/INTERFACES.md
